direction: right
title: Java Fail-Fast Iteration & modCount Detection Mechanics

Stage1: 1. Iterator Initialization {
  style.fill: "#0B132B"
  style.stroke: "#0284C7"
  init: "it = list.iterator()"
  state: "expectedModCount = list.modCount = 5"
}

Stage2: 2. Direct Modification {
  style.fill: "#1C1917"
  style.stroke: "#F59E0B"
  mutation: "list.add('Element') -> list.modCount++ (6)"
  desync: "list.modCount (6) != it.expectedModCount (5)"
}

Stage3: 3. Fail-Fast Exception {
  style.fill: "#1C1917"
  style.stroke: "#EF4444"
  check: "it.next() checks: modCount == expectedModCount"
  error: "Throws ConcurrentModificationException"
}

SafePattern: Safe Alternative {
  style.fill: "#06201B"
  style.stroke: "#10B981"
  solution: "Use it.remove(): syncs expectedModCount = modCount"
}

Stage1 -> Stage2: Mutation occurs during loop
Stage2 -> Stage3: Next it.next() call triggers check
